<pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I546c09a5672d33062f1f60fc38e2efa6a8ef6c01" commit="a18fae453443037038fe2eaee40396c03ecb6f72" commit_message="UPSTREAM: mm/slab: put the freelist at the end of slab page  Currently, the freelist is at the front of slab page.  This requires extra space to meet object alignment requirement.  If we put the freelist at the end of a slab page, objects could start at page boundary and will be at correct alignment.  This is possible because freelist has no alignment constraint itself.  This gives us two benefits: It removes extra memory space for the freelist alignment and remove complex calculation at cache initialization step.  I can't think notable drawback here.  I mentioned that this would reduce extra memory space, but, this benefit is rather theoretical because it can be applied to very few cases. Following is the example cache type that can get benefit from this change.    size align num before after     32    8  124  4100  4092     64    8   63  4103  4095     88    8   46  4102  4094    272    8   15  4103  4095    408    8   10  4098  4090     32   16  124  4108  4092     64   16   63  4111  4095     32   32  124  4124  4092     64   32   63  4127  4095     96   32   42  4106  4074  before means whole size for objects and aligned freelist before applying patch and after shows the result of this patch.  Since before is more than 4096, number of object should decrease and memory waste happens.  Anyway, this patch removes complex calculation so looks beneficial to me.  [akpm@linux-foundation.org: fix kerneldoc] Signed-off-by: Joonsoo Kim &lt;iamjoonsoo.kim@lge.com&gt; Acked-by: Christoph Lameter &lt;cl@linux.com&gt; Cc: Pekka Enberg &lt;penberg@kernel.org&gt; Cc: David Rientjes &lt;rientjes@google.com&gt; Cc: Joonsoo Kim &lt;iamjoonsoo.kim@lge.com&gt; Cc: Jesper Dangaard Brouer &lt;brouer@redhat.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton &lt;akpm@linux-foundation.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Linus Torvalds &lt;torvalds@linux-foundation.org&gt;  BUG=chromium:605531 BUG=chromium:545468 TEST=build and run with USE=&quot;allocator_slab kasan&quot;  (cherry picked from commit 2e6b3602168797fd4d80d86d208c4ba8fcfa3b8b) Signed-off-by: Alexander Potapenko &lt;glider@google.com&gt;  Change-Id: I546c09a5672d33062f1f60fc38e2efa6a8ef6c01 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/339963 Commit-Ready: Alexander Potapenko &lt;glider@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Alexander Potapenko &lt;glider@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Sonny Rao &lt;sonnyrao@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Alexander Potapenko &lt;glider@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="339963" owner_email="glider@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/63/339963/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I0ef7871bbf6e7592c5a76aa7f8dfcae3254fd695" commit="c8fc9f1c34ec2cd372a271a26df3bc9e5a4988a5" commit_message="UPSTREAM: mm/slab: clean up cache type determination  Current cache type determination code is open-code and looks not understandable.  Following patch will introduce one more cache type and it would make code more complex.  So, before it happens, this patch abstracts these codes.  Signed-off-by: Joonsoo Kim &lt;iamjoonsoo.kim@lge.com&gt; Cc: Christoph Lameter &lt;cl@linux.com&gt; Cc: Pekka Enberg &lt;penberg@kernel.org&gt; Cc: David Rientjes &lt;rientjes@google.com&gt; Cc: Joonsoo Kim &lt;iamjoonsoo.kim@lge.com&gt; Cc: Jesper Dangaard Brouer &lt;brouer@redhat.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton &lt;akpm@linux-foundation.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Linus Torvalds &lt;torvalds@linux-foundation.org&gt;  BUG=chromium:605531 BUG=chromium:545468 TEST=build and run with USE=&quot;allocator_slab kasan&quot;  (cherry picked from commit 158e319bba59e890c3920ce6d827c188287bae84) Signed-off-by: Alexander Potapenko &lt;glider@google.com&gt;  Change-Id: I0ef7871bbf6e7592c5a76aa7f8dfcae3254fd695 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/339964 Commit-Ready: Alexander Potapenko &lt;glider@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Alexander Potapenko &lt;glider@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Sonny Rao &lt;sonnyrao@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="339964" owner_email="glider@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/64/339964/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I367fb2502fe02c6264cf543349bfed74dc00c0ed" commit="eaf2749fd50a01b08f8c354f21486d0378491987" commit_message="UPSTREAM: mm/slab: make criteria for off slab determination robust and simple  To become an off slab, there are some constraints to avoid bootstrapping problem and recursive call.  This can be avoided differently by simply checking that corresponding kmalloc cache is ready and it's not a off slab.  It would be more robust because static size checking can be affected by cache size change or architecture type but dynamic checking isn't.  One check 'freelist_cache-&gt;size &gt; cachep-&gt;size / 2' is added to check benefit of choosing off slab, because, now, there is no size constraint which ensures enough advantage when selecting off slab.  Signed-off-by: Joonsoo Kim &lt;iamjoonsoo.kim@lge.com&gt; Cc: Christoph Lameter &lt;cl@linux.com&gt; Cc: Pekka Enberg &lt;penberg@kernel.org&gt; Cc: David Rientjes &lt;rientjes@google.com&gt; Cc: Joonsoo Kim &lt;iamjoonsoo.kim@lge.com&gt; Cc: Jesper Dangaard Brouer &lt;brouer@redhat.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton &lt;akpm@linux-foundation.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Linus Torvalds &lt;torvalds@linux-foundation.org&gt;  BUG=chromium:605531 BUG=chromium:545468 TEST=build and run with USE=&quot;allocator_slab kasan&quot;  (cherry picked from commit 3217fd9bdf0017bd0847939f67d52a9c71d8fc56) Signed-off-by: Alexander Potapenko &lt;glider@google.com&gt;  Change-Id: I367fb2502fe02c6264cf543349bfed74dc00c0ed Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/339965 Commit-Ready: Alexander Potapenko &lt;glider@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Alexander Potapenko &lt;glider@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Sonny Rao &lt;sonnyrao@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="339965" owner_email="glider@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/65/339965/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I97c180284537967217beb38300fcbe6b3971bafa" commit="841b4528a87f622b0f5e41bd6caa9073ef7e07c4" commit_message="UPSTREAM: ASoC: mediatek: Add second I2S on mt8173-rt5650 machine driver  This patch adds second I2S connection to rt5650 codec for capture path on mt8173-rt5650 machine driver.  Signed-off-by: PC Liao &lt;pc.liao@mediatek.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Mark Brown &lt;broonie@kernel.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit d349caeb05104ef01392abc6c7cfc8ab516c7be4)  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49521 BUG=chrome-os-partner:51725 TEST=build and boot elm-rev0 TEST=play and record sound =&gt; Sound works CQ-DEPEND=CL:340266  Change-Id: I97c180284537967217beb38300fcbe6b3971bafa Signed-off-by: PC Liao &lt;pc.liao@mediatek.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/330302 Reviewed-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="330302" owner_email="pc.liao@mediatek.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="12" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/02/330302/12" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I5f959f00dd91864843f6ee0119350615437b7da9" commit="dce31d6dab2f8b9e341ea4352c5ff7e22d9e591d" commit_message="CHROMIUM: arm64: dts: mt8173-elm: update sound node  The latest audio machine driver adds &quot;codec-capture&quot; node to handle &quot;sound-dai&quot; property. This patch makes the correlated change (CL:330302).  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49521 BUG=chrome-os-partner:51725 TEST=build and boot elm-rev0 TEST=play and record sound =&gt; Sound works  Change-Id: I5f959f00dd91864843f6ee0119350615437b7da9 Signed-off-by: PC Liao &lt;pc.liao@mediatek.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/340266 Reviewed-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="340266" owner_email="pc.liao@mediatek.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/66/340266/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.02" change_id="I017207b2d4108de150853f421aa7bcfd0e12e9a4" commit="864d780ac857aa6f58b2d1f9cabfd2a697221a8f" commit_message="util: ipq40xx: Scripts to combine SBL and Coreboot ELFs  The IPQ40xx Primary Boot Loader (PBL, i.e. Boot-ROM) expects an ELF in the boot medium to load and boot. These scripts combine the Secondary Boot Loader (SBL) and Coreboot ELF to an image as expected by the PBL.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49249 TEST=Able to boot and reach depthcharge BRANCH=none  Change-Id: I017207b2d4108de150853f421aa7bcfd0e12e9a4 Signed-off-by: Varadarajan Narayanan &lt;varada@codeaurora.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/340181 Commit-Ready: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="340181" owner_email="varada@codeaurora.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/81/340181/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeo