ile and should not be located in our read-only /etc/cups/. Move these under PrinterRoot as well.  Not pitched upstream yet, since upstream rejected the initial patch.  This also fixes a few other oversights, where CUPS would still look for PPDs in /etc/cups/ppd/PRINTERNAME.ppd instead of $PrinterRoot/ppd/PRINTERNAME.ppd.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:47758,chrome-os-partner:49267 TEST=`cups-browsed`; make sure cupsd can write to      $PrinterRoot/subscriptions.conf  Change-Id: I82e45b80b090150969083c7bd2bc16695e0b22c4 Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/334319 Commit-Ready: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Sean Kau &lt;skau@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Sean Kau &lt;skau@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="334319" owner_email="briannorris@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/19/334319/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6c2dbbe060437de49075d74bd2179cb3a17fdd06" commit="8465bdfcd2a89c033aed2f9df112ba83cd52a57f" commit_message="arc-libs: Update to _p3 with latest libdrm include files  Previous _p2 used an older version of the libdrm include files, which is lacking some definitions necessary for intel.  BUG=b:28030733 TEST=Build arc-mesa  Change-Id: I6c2dbbe060437de49075d74bd2179cb3a17fdd06 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/340330 Commit-Ready: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ben Cheng &lt;bccheng@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="340330" owner_email="drinkcat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromi